\subsection{Scientific Interpretation}
\noindent
The roadmap defines the experimental gates required for empirical 
verification. Each criterion is binary, measurable, and falsifiable. 
Until these phases are completed, the AITFE remains a theoretically 
validated propulsion concept rather than an empirically demonstrated 
engine.

\begin{lemma}[Empirical Requirement]
Simulation does not constitute empirical proof.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Empirical validation requires physical fabrication, cryogenic antimatter 
confinement, fusion pulse diagnostics, direct energy conversion 
measurements, and independent replication. None of these have yet been 
performed.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Conclusion}
\noindent
The AITFE framework is mathematically validated and supported by a 
rigorous TRL roadmap. Empirical verification remains the next scientific 
milestone.